         <div type="bio">
            <p>English journalist, reviewer, and editor. His weekly column, “A Literary Letter”, surveyed recent publications from a conservative point of view. In it he judged  <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> to be “the maddest, muddiest, most loathsome book issued in our own or any other time” (<name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">The Sphere</name> 90, no. 1172 [8 July 1922]: 50). <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
